# Menus: a right click opens the menu of what it landed on — the page, a
# link, a picture, a selection, a field, a tab, the address bar — and the
# button at the toolbar's right end opens the window's main menu. The page
# hears contextmenu first and may keep the shell's menu away, unless the
# reader holds Shift. The keyboard works a menu too, and an open menu
# holds the pointer: a press beside it closes it and does nothing more.
resize 900 600
open data:text/html,<title>Menus</title><body style="margin:0"><p style="margin:10px">Plain words and a <a href="data:text/html,<title>Second</title><p>Landed.">link</a> to follow.</p><p style="margin:10px" oncontextmenu="event.preventDefault();document.title='asked'">guarded</p><img width=40 height=40 style="position:absolute;left:20px;top:120px" src="data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mP8z8BQDwAEhQGAhKmMIQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg=="><input name=q value=hello style="position:absolute;left:20px;top:200px;width:200px"><div style="height:2000px"></div>
assert-title Menus
assert-menu

# The page's own menu: Back leads to the blank page the tab opened on, and
# there is nowhere forward to go.
right-click-text Plain
assert-menus 1
assert-menu Back | (Forward) | Reload | - | Select all | - | View page source | - | Inspect
key Escape
assert-menus 0

# A press beside an open menu closes it, and that is all it does: the link
# under the press is not followed. The wheel moves nothing meanwhile.
right-click-text Plain
wheel -3
assert-scroll 0
click-text link
assert-menus 0
assert-title Menus

# A link's menu. Its address goes to the clipboard as the page wrote it.
right-click-text link
assert-menu Open link in new tab | Open link in new container tab > | - | Copy link address | - | Inspect
menu Copy link address
assert-menus 0
assert-clipboard data:text/html,<title>Second</title><p>Landed.
right-click-text link
menu Open link in new tab
# The tab opens behind the page the reader is on, beside it.
assert-tab-titles [Menus] | Second
select-tab 1
assert-title Second
close-tab
assert-tabs 1
assert-title Menus

# The submenu opens beside its item, and its choice opens the link in a
# tab of that container — behind, as well.
right-click-text link
menu Open link in new container tab
assert-menus 2
assert-menu No container | Personal | Work | Banking | Shopping
menu Work
assert-menus 0
assert-tab-titles [Menus] | Second
select-tab 1
assert-container Work
assert-title Second
close-tab

# Ctrl with a click opens the link in a tab of its own, behind.
ctrl-click-text link
assert-tab-titles [Menus] | Second
select-tab 1
assert-title Second
close-tab
assert-title Menus

# The pointer over an item that has a submenu opens it; over another item
# it closes again. Escape closes the innermost menu, then the rest.
right-click-text link
menu-hover 0 1
assert-menus 2
menu-hover 0 0
assert-menus 1
menu-hover 0 1
assert-menus 2
assert-golden goldens/menus-link.png
key Escape
assert-menus 1
key Escape
assert-menus 0

# The keyboard: the Menu key opens the page's menu, the arrows pass over
# what cannot be chosen and wrap, Right opens a submenu and Left closes it,
# a letter goes to the item that begins with it, Enter chooses.
key Menu
assert-menus 1
key Down
key Down
key Enter
assert-menus 0
assert-title Menus
assert-status Done
key shift+F10
assert-menus 1
type i
key Enter
assert-inspected html
key F12
right-click-text link
key Down
key Down
key Right
assert-menus 2
key Down
key Left
assert-menus 1
key Right
key Down
key Down
key Enter
assert-tab-titles [Menus] | Second
select-tab 1
assert-container Work
close-tab

# A page that answers contextmenu itself keeps the shell's menu away;
# Shift with the click shows it regardless.
right-click-text guarded
assert-menus 0
assert-title asked
shift-right-click-text guarded
assert-menus 1
key Escape

# A selection brings Copy.
select-text words
right-click-text words
assert-menu Copy | - | Inspect
menu Copy
assert-clipboard words
key Escape

# A picture's menu. Saving it puts it in the downloads folder, as a download.
right-click 40 216
assert-menu Open image in new tab | Copy image address | Save image | - | Inspect
menu Save image
assert-status Saved download
assert-status .png to 
right-click 40 216
menu Copy image address
assert-clipboard data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAAAAEAAAABCAYAAAAfFcSJAAAADUlEQVR42mP8z8BQDwAEhQGAhKmMIQAAAABJRU5ErkJggg==

# A field takes the focus and offers Paste; it has no selection of its own,
# so nothing to cut or copy.
set-clipboard there
right-click 100 288
assert-focused q
assert-menu (Cut) | (Copy) | Paste | - | Inspect
menu Paste
assert-value q hellothere
key Escape

# A tab's menu: the tabs beside it close, the one asked about stays.
new-tab
new-tab
assert-tabs 3
right-click-tab 0
assert-menu New tab | - | Reload tab | Duplicate tab | - | Close tab | Close other tabs | Close tabs to the right | - | Reopen closed tab
menu Close tabs to the right
assert-tabs 1
assert-title asked
right-click-tab 0
assert-menu New tab | - | Reload tab | Duplicate tab | - | Close tab | (Close other tabs) | (Close tabs to the right) | - | Reopen closed tab
menu New tab
assert-tabs 2
right-click-tab 0
menu Close other tabs
assert-tabs 1
assert-title asked

# The address bar's menu: Cut empties it into the clipboard, Paste and go
# navigates to what the clipboard holds.
right-click-address
assert-focus address
assert-menu Cut | Copy | Paste | Paste and go | - | Select all
menu Cut
assert-address
set-clipboard data:text/html,<title>Pasted</title><p>Went there.
right-click-address
assert-menu (Cut) | (Copy) | Paste | Paste and go | - | (Select all)
menu Paste and go
assert-title Pasted
back
assert-title Menus

# The main menu, hung from its button: the theme in use is checked, a
# theme chosen is put on, and a second press on the button closes it.
main-menu
assert-menus 1
assert-menu New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | Reader mode | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | Developer tools | View page source | - | About Sashfold | Quit
main-menu
assert-menus 0
main-menu
menu Themes
assert-menu High Contrast | Nord | *Sashfold | Sashfold Light | Solarized Dark
assert-golden goldens/menus-main.png
menu Nord
assert-theme Nord
main-menu
menu Themes
assert-menu High Contrast | *Nord | Sashfold | Sashfold Light | Solarized Dark
menu Sashfold
assert-theme Sashfold
main-menu
menu Developer tools
main-menu
assert-menu New tab | New container tab > | - | Find in page | Reader mode | - | Themes > | Command palette | - | *Developer tools | View page source | - | About Sashfold | Quit
menu Developer tools
main-menu
menu New container tab
menu Banking
assert-container Banking
close-tab

# The button pressed and let go where it is leaves the menu open; held
# down, the pointer slid to an item, and let go there, it chooses the item.
press 880 56
assert-menus 1
release
assert-menus 1
key Escape
press 880 56
menu-hover 0 0
release
assert-menus 0
assert-tabs 2
close-tab

# A menu opens with its first item a hair from the pointer: a click that
# shakes onto it chooses nothing, a slide onto it does.
press 205 96 3
assert-menu Open link in new tab | Open link in new container tab > | - | Copy link address | - | Inspect
move 210 101
release 3
assert-menus 1
assert-tabs 1
key Escape
press 205 96 3
move 260 115
release 3
assert-menus 0
assert-tab-titles [Menus] | Second
close-tab 1

# Quit asks the window to close.
assert-window-request none
main-menu
menu Quit
assert-window-request close
key ctrl+shift+q
assert-window-request close
